ICE-01 - the compiler broke its own rules

WHAT   The compiler hit a condition it promises is unreachable:
       a stage failed before its output could be produced.
WHY    The compiler's job is a verdict for every input; bail-outs
       mean a bug in the compiler, not in your program.
BAD    any input that ends in a compiler crash
GOOD   the same input getting a diagnostic, or compiling
NOTE   Please report it: the source that triggered it is the
       most useful thing you can attach.
